To Whom It May Concern:

Pursuant to the Pennsylvania Right to Know Act, I hereby request the following records:

I request records of any counts of pedestrians at specific locations in the city from 2019 through 2025, showing where, on what date or dates and at what times each count was taken, and how many pedestrians were counted.

1. Pedestrian counts. All counts of pedestrians at specific locations in the city taken by or for the agency from January 1, 2019 through December 31, 2025. This includes, for example:

manual or video-based counts of people walking on sidewalks or crossing at intersections, including turning-movement counts that record crosswalk volumes;
automated pedestrian counters (for example, infrared or camera-based sensors), short-term or permanent;
counts made for specific projects, studies, before-and-after evaluations or count programs;
pedestrian counts that the agency received from other public agencies, business improvement districts or consultants.
2. What each record should show. For each count, records sufficient to show:

the location: coordinates, or the street and cross streets or block, and a site or station identifier if one is used;
the date of the count (day, month and year); for counts that ran over several days or continuously (for example, multi-day or permanent counters), the first and last date and the date of each interval;
the start and end time of each counting interval;
the number of pedestrians in each interval, at the finest time interval recorded (for example, each 15 minutes or each hour);
the count method (manual, video, or automated sensor type);
whether pedestrians are counted separately from people on bicycles or scooters;
whether the values are raw counts or adjusted or estimated figures (for example, factored to an annual average);
any flags for missing, partial or faulty intervals.
If this information exists only in raw count files, field sheets, sensor exports or reports delivered by a count contractor, I request copies of those files.

3. Documentation. For each file provided, any data dictionary, codebook, field definitions, methodology notes or other documentation that explains its columns, codes and units.

I am not requesting video recordings or any personal information.

I would prefer records in their original electronic format (CSV, Excel or similar) rather than PDF scans, released on a rolling basis as they are ready. If some of these records are held by another agency, I would be grateful to know which one.

This request supports academic research that checks whether anonymized mobile-device location data track pedestrian activity. The dates and locations of counts are needed to compare each count with the mobile data for the same place and day.

The requested documents will be made available to the general public, and this request is not being made for commercial purposes.

In the event that there are fees, I would be grateful if you would inform me of the total charges in advance of fulfilling my request. I would prefer the request filled electronically, by e-mail attachment if available or CD-ROM if not.

Thank you in advance for your anticipated cooperation in this matter. I look forward to receiving your response to this request within 5 business days, as the statute requires.

Sincerely,

Jonathan Mummolo

RI Department of Administration

