Hello,

&nbsp;This correspondence regards your public records request dated (10/06/25), and identified by the City as (25-14672), where you sough the following:



[see request]

&nbsp;

My office has located a number of non-exempt responsive documents in paper form and those documents are available for your personal inspection. Please contact my office should you wish to set up an inspection. There is no cost to inspect the records in person. If you are unable or unwilling to inspect in person, or if you would prefer copies of the non-exempt responsive records – then under the law the City “may require advance payment of the fees before making copies of public records.” NMSA 1978, § 14-2-9(C)(5). Prior to copying and mailing the records, my office will require advance payment of the copying fees ($1.00 per page) as well as the costs associated with mailing the set of documents to you.&nbsp;See&nbsp;NMSA 1978, § 14-2-9(C)(4) (“may charge the actual costs associated with transmitting copies of public records by mail”).&nbsp;

&nbsp;

We have determined there will be (35) pages and we will require advance payment of the copying and mailing costs. At your request, my office can provide you with an invoice for those costs. Should you desire the copies then my office will mail those records after we have received payment. Please know that this is just a deposit, there may be additional fees associated with your request.

&nbsp;

I hope this email provides you enough information so that you can let me know how you wish to proceed on you public records request. I look forward to hearing from you.

&nbsp;

Please let me know if you have any questions.

&nbsp;

Sincerely,

&nbsp;

Donald Byrd

